 "summary": "Mostly no. Price after a bottom wick did no better than after a random candle on 4h or daily, and on 1h the lead shows at 20 candles only. The result that holds up runs against shorts: after a top wick started, price rose more than after a random candle, by 0.6% on 1h and 2.25% on 4h.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Going long after a bottom wick starts (threshold 1)",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "On 1h it beat random entries at 20 candles only, and was chance at 10, 50 and 100. It fires in volatile candles in a window that rose, so this is timing, not direction. On 4h and daily it was inside the luck band."
  },
  {
   "use": "Going long while the bottom wick level holds",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "No better than random entries on 1h or 4h, at threshold 2 with a 200-bar level. Daily has too few separate moves to judge."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting after a top wick starts (threshold 1)",
