   "text": "Worse than random on 1h and 4h. Price kept rising after long upper wicks, at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles, and the result holds without its strongest stretch."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting while the top wick level holds",
   "verdict": "worse",
   "text": "Worse than random on 1h at 10 and 20 candles, then chance at 50 and 100. On 4h it was inside the luck band."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, a bottom wick starting at threshold 1 gave 1,547 entries in 1,225 separate moves. Twenty candles later price was 0.31% ahead of random entries, just above a luck band of -0.19% to 0.21%. At 10, 50 and 100 candles it was chance. These signals fire in volatile candles, and in a window that rose, price moved more after them. That is when they fire, not a read on direction.",
  "The coins split. On SOL 1h, price was 1.07% ahead of random after 20 candles. The lead shows at 10, 50 and 100 candles and holds without signals on Sep 8, 2021. It is the same volatility timing, not a directional edge. On BTC 1h price was 0.2% behind random, but only because of signals on Jun 12–15, 2022, when Celsius froze withdrawals. ETH sat inside the band.",
  "Top wicks are the clearer result. A short after a top wick started at threshold 1 did 0.6% worse than random after 20 candles on 1h, across 1,159 separate moves, and 2.25% worse on 4h. Both hold without their strongest stretch and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles. On 1h each coin was worse than random. On 4h SOL was 4.36% worse and BTC 1.34% worse, while ETH sat inside the band.",
  "On 1h, bottom wicks at threshold 1 gave 1,547 entries against 290 at threshold 2, and threshold 2 lands inside the luck band on 1h and 4h. Holding a 200-bar bottom wick level was within 0.03% of random on 1h and 0.01% on 4h. Holding a top wick level did 0.34% worse than random for shorts on 1h, but only at 10 and 20 candles.",
  "Daily candles give too few separate moves to judge most settings. Where a pooled daily result exists, it sits inside the luck band: price was 3.19% ahead after bottom wicks and 4.3% behind for shorts after top wicks, both chance.",
  "For a long bot on 1h, a bottom wick start adds at most a short-lived lift tied to volatile candles, so treat it as a filter beside a trend condition rather than a trigger. A take profit that needs more than 20 candles to fill gets nothing from it. For a short bot, a fresh top wick is a reason to leave the setting out: price kept rising after it on 1h and 4h."
